![](/guides/img/admin-01-today-desktop-ea48309c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin; pins: 1 22.9 65.0, 2 61.8 65.6, 5 76.4 56.1, 6 84.4 24.7, 7 58.3 37.8")

## The menu

Today and Bookings open to show their pages; Cars, People, Marketing, Money and Settings are one link each, which opens the area''s main page with a row of its pages on top. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button that says where you are.

| Menu | Pages (the row on top, then a page''s tabs) |
| --- | --- |
| Today | To do, Overview, Staff tasks, Visitors |
| Bookings | Trips: Bookings (Now and All bookings), Requests and offers (with Chauffeur), Calendar. Customers: Live chat, Reviews. Problems: Damage and claims (tabs Damage, Incidents, Claims) |
| Cars (opens on Vehicles) | Vehicles (tabs All cars, Fleet tracking, Rates for many cars, Calendar sync, Retire or delete), Listings (tabs Listings, Similar cars), Maintenance |
| Money (opens on Payments, By day) | Payments (tabs By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Disputes, Reconciliation), Owner money (tabs Invoices, Debits, Statements, Payouts), Tolls and tickets, Company accounts (tabs Monthly statements, Company model, Expenses), Insurers (tabs Rates, Invoices), Staff pay (tabs Commissions, Field pay) |
| People (opens on Owners) | Owners (tabs Owners, Paid and signed, Owner forms, Add a car), Applications, Partners (tabs Rental partners, Referral partners), Renters (tabs Renters, Leads), Staff (tabs Staff and roles, Academy, Hiring, Portals and view as), Investors |
| Marketing (opens on Ads) | Ads (tabs Marketplace, Ad listings, Posted ads, Social drafts, Listing channels, Bookings by channel), Owner recruitment (tabs Recruitment, Owner pipeline) |
| Settings (opens on Settings) | Settings (every setting in six sections, with a search box), Logs (tabs Emails, Blocked addresses, Changes, Data access) |

![On a phone: press Menu (1), then a group (2), then the page (3).](/guides/img/admin-31-menu-phone-667dc2fd.jpg "phone; size: 390 715; pins: 1 10.3 28.7, 2 76.9 42.4, 3 76.9 48.3")

## Tabs on a page

A menu link such as **Money** opens a page with a row on top: the area''s name in capitals, then its pages (Payments, Owner money, Tolls and tickets...). The page you are on is black. A page with tabs (such as **Owner money**: Invoices, Debits, Statements, Payouts) has a second row under it, the tab you are on outlined in red. On a phone each row slides sideways.

1. Press a tab to change what the page shows. Each tab has its own address, so a link or a bookmark to a tab opens that tab.
2. An old address (an email or a bookmark from before November 2026, such as Owner invoices or the Audit log) opens the page and the tab that now holds it.
3. Ctrl+K lists every tab too: type Debits or Field pay and press Enter.

## Search

The search box sits at the top of the menu, on every page.

1. Type a booking number (CC-1042), a car code (CC-7F3A, on every car page and fleet card), a plate, a VIN, or a name or email address.
2. Press **Search** (or Enter). Results come in groups: bookings, cars, owners, partners and renters. Open one to go to its page.
3. To go to a page instead, press Ctrl+K (Cmd+K on a Mac) or **Jump to a page** under the search box, type a few letters (Payouts, Program settings) and press Enter. The first line searches the records for what you typed.

![](/guides/img/admin-32-search-desktop-ca548a70.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 420; address: carmacars.ca/admin/search?q=CC-10065; pins: 1 7.4 45.2, 2 95.0 46.9")

## Keyboard shortcuts

Press g, then a letter. Press / to jump to the search box, and Ctrl+K to jump to any page.

| Keys | Opens | Keys | Opens |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| g t | To do | g v | Cars (Vehicles) |
| g r | Requests | g o | People (Owners) |
| g b | Bookings | g m | Money (Payments) |
| g c | Calendar | g k | Staff tasks |
| g s | Settings | / | Search |
| Ctrl K | Jump to a page | Esc | Close it |
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Admin opens on To do: the day&#39;s counts at the top, then what needs you now, most urgent first. The menu groups every screen into seven groups: Today, Bookings, Cars, People, Marketing, Money and Settings. Pages on one subject are one menu link with a row of tabs on top (for example Money &gt; Owner money: Invoices, Debits, Statements, Payouts). Search finds any booking, car or person, and Ctrl+K jumps to any page.</p><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-to-do" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">To do</h2><p class="gd-p">Start every shift here. Each line says what to do and why, and its button opens a small pop-up that does it, already filled in. Nothing to remember and no menu to search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each piece of work is its own line (work of one kind for several cars is one line, such as Add real photos (72 cars); its button opens the list), marked Now, Today or When you can: a car the insurer has not confirmed, a car not on the site, a renter&#39;s documents to check, a visitor waiting in live chat, a booking request, a change a renter asked for, an owner application, an owner invoice waiting for payment, the first and last month an owner paid after their invoices were voided, the terms agreed with an owner still on the standard grid, documents an owner has not signed, an official form to check, a plate to check, a car showing sample photos, and any task of the Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press the line&#39;s button: Mark insured, Set rates and publish, Review documents, Record payment, Record what they paid, Enter the terms, Record paper signature, Checked: use for owners, Open the chat, and so on. A line you do not need has Not needed or These are correct. The pop-up is filled in; check it and confirm. The line disappears once the work is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under the lines, the counts with one button each (failed payments, agreements to countersign, tolls, listings, insurance, staff commissions, prices typed by hand, sales claims, Turo emails). A count with nothing waiting moves to the bottom, under &quot;more with nothing waiting&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">While no assistant holds customer service, sales, finance or fleet (the live verification&#39;s test accounts do not count), their tasks come to To do too, and so do their emails, to rent@carmacars.ca.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Beside the list (under it on a phone): today&#39;s pickups (ready or not ready), today&#39;s returns (due or late) and today&#39;s chauffeur bookings, by time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> for the money, fleet and queue figures, the alerts and the team&#39;s sales for the month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The dark band at the top counts the day, each count one tap from its page: requests waiting (with how long the oldest has waited, red past the reply target), pickups and returns today, payments to chase, deposits to settle, staff tasks open and alerts. A count that needs you now is red and says so.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-01-today-desktop-ea48309c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:65%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.8%;top:65.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.4%;top:56.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.4%;top:24.7%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:58.3%;top:37.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-the-menu" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The menu</h2><p class="gd-p">Today and Bookings open to show their pages; Cars, People, Marketing, Money and Settings are one link each, which opens the area&#39;s main page with a row of its pages on top. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button that says where you are.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Menu</th><th scope="col">Pages (the row on top, then a page&#39;s tabs)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Today</td><td>To do, Overview, Staff tasks, Visitors</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings</td><td>Trips: Bookings (Now and All bookings), Requests and offers (with Chauffeur), Calendar. Customers: Live chat, Reviews. Problems: Damage and claims (tabs Damage, Incidents, Claims)</td></tr><tr><td>Cars (opens on Vehicles)</td><td>Vehicles (tabs All cars, Fleet tracking, Rates for many cars, Calendar sync, Retire or delete), Listings (tabs Listings, Similar cars), Maintenance</td></tr><tr><td>Money (opens on Payments, By day)</td><td>Payments (tabs By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Disputes, Reconciliation), Owner money (tabs Invoices, Debits, Statements, Payouts), Tolls and tickets, Company accounts (tabs Monthly statements, Company model, Expenses), Insurers (tabs Rates, Invoices), Staff pay (tabs Commissions, Field pay)</td></tr><tr><td>People (opens on Owners)</td><td>Owners (tabs Owners, Paid and signed, Owner forms, Add a car), Applications, Partners (tabs Rental partners, Referral partners), Renters (tabs Renters, Leads), Staff (tabs Staff and roles, Academy, Hiring, Portals and view as), Investors</td></tr><tr><td>Marketing (opens on Ads)</td><td>Ads (tabs Marketplace, Ad listings, Posted ads, Social drafts, Listing channels, Bookings by channel), Owner recruitment (tabs Recruitment, Owner pipeline)</td></tr><tr><td>Settings (opens on Settings)</td><td>Settings (every setting in six sections, with a search box), Logs (tabs Emails, Blocked addresses, Changes, Data access)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/715"><img src="/guides/img/admin-31-menu-phone-667dc2fd.jpg" alt="On a phone: press Menu (1), then a group (2), then the page (3)." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="715"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.3%;top:28.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:42.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:48.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>On a phone: press Menu (1), then a group (2), then the page (3).</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-tabs-on-a-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tabs on a page</h2><p class="gd-p">A menu link such as <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> opens a page with a row on top: the area&#39;s name in capitals, then its pages (Payments, Owner money, Tolls and tickets...). The page you are on is black. A page with tabs (such as <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>: Invoices, Debits, Statements, Payouts) has a second row under it, the tab you are on outlined in red. On a phone each row slides sideways.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press a tab to change what the page shows. Each tab has its own address, so a link or a bookmark to a tab opens that tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An old address (an email or a bookmark from before November 2026, such as Owner invoices or the Audit log) opens the page and the tab that now holds it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Ctrl+K lists every tab too: type Debits or Field pay and press Enter.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-search" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search</h2><p class="gd-p">The search box sits at the top of the menu, on every page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type a booking number (CC-1042), a car code (CC-7F3A, on every car page and fleet card), a plate, a VIN, or a name or email address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> (or Enter). Results come in groups: bookings, cars, owners, partners and renters. Open one to go to its page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To go to a page instead, press Ctrl+K (Cmd+K on a Mac) or <b class="gd-ui">Jump to a page</b> under the search box, type a few letters (Payouts, Program settings) and press Enter. The first line searches the records for what you typed.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/search?q=CC-10065</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/420"><img src="/guides/img/admin-32-search-desktop-ca548a70.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="420"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:7.4%;top:45.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95%;top:46.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-keyboard-shortcuts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Keyboard shortcuts</h2><p class="gd-p">Press g, then a letter. Press / to jump to the search box, and Ctrl+K to jump to any page.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Keys</th><th scope="col">Opens</th><th scope="col">Keys</th><th scope="col">Opens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>g t</td><td>To do</td><td>g v</td><td>Cars (Vehicles)</td></tr><tr><td>g r</td><td>Requests</td><td>g o</td><td>People (Owners)</td></tr><tr><td>g b</td><td>Bookings</td><td>g m</td><td>Money (Payments)</td></tr><tr><td>g c</td><td>Calendar</td><td>g k</td><td>Staff tasks</td></tr><tr><td>g s</td><td>Settings</td><td>/</td><td>Search</td></tr><tr><td>Ctrl K</td><td>Jump to a page</td><td>Esc</td><td>Close it</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'people-and-access', 'chapter', 'getting-around-admin', 'Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.

## Portals and sign-in

Open **People** > **Portals and view as**. Every portal has a card.

1. Each card links to **Its sign-in page**, the address to send that person.
2. Choose a person in the list on the card.
3. Press **Open as this person** to see that portal as they see it.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 65.9 30.2, 2 58.1 39.4, 3 51.6 45.6")

## Invite a person

Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.

1. Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.
2. Fill in the Name and Email.
3. For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.
4. Press **Invite**. The link in the email works for 24 hours.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 360; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 18.8 40.8, 2 50.0 40.8, 3 18.8 66.7, 4 9.8 87.8")

> Tip: Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People > Owners and People > Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.

## Add an investor

1. Open **People** > **Investors** and press **Add an investor**.
2. Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).
3. Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer''s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).
4. Invite now is ticked: press **Add and invite**. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.

## Send a password link

For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.

1. Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.
2. On their row, press **Send password link**. They get "Reset your CarmaCars password", valid for 24 hours.
3. **View as (...)** on the same row opens their portal, read only.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 440; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 74.8 6.6, 2 68.2 28.6, 3 84.1 28.6")

## View as: see what someone sees

1. A red banner says "Viewing as Name (email), read only." on every page.
2. Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.
3. Press **Exit** to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.

![](/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 620; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 48.6 4.5, 3 94.4 4.5")

> Watch out: Can''t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.

## The audit log

**Settings** > **Audit log** shows who changed what, and when.

1. Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.
2. Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.
3. Search by table, record id or value.

![](/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/audit; pins: 1 22.6 31.1, 2 39.0 46.4, 3 89.6 20.7")

## Staff and roles

**People** > **Staff** opens Staff and roles.

1. Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then **Invite**.
2. Each row has **Send password link**, **View as (...)** and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).
3. Press **End access** to close their staff portal at once. **Restore** undoes it.

![](/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 780; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff; pins: 1 20.8 59.0, 2 94.4 86.7, 3 83.3 92.6")

## Admin access

**Settings** > **All settings**, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.

1. The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site''s nightly checks sign in with.
2. Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.
3. Change the list only if the business''s Admin address changes.

## Staff scorecards

See how each assistant is doing against the targets.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Scorecard**.
2. By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 350; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 2 21.1 42.9")

## Sales by staff member

See each person''s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Sales**. Press **By week** or **By month**.
2. The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.
3. Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.
4. A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press **Reassign** beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.
5. **Commission rate** gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). **Reverse** beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.
6. Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. **Home address** here changes it if it is wrong.
7. The whole team: **Today** > **Overview**, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press **Show**.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to | Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |
', 'People and access', 'Portals and sign-in, invitations, password links, View as, staff and scorecards.',
