wner until they answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Not a fit? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>, write the Reason the owner reads, and press <b class="gd-ui">Decline the application</b>. The owner is emailed for each car.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:67.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.9%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:49.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says &quot;Entered by staff&quot; and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Notes on the page are for staff only: <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b> keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> tab, or <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on an owner&#39;s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner&#39;s terms, or their other car&#39;s; change them for this car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). How the owner signs: by email, or on paper.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and set it up</b>. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, <b class="gd-ui">Send the set-up email again</b> sends the owner the email with a fresh link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b> shows their portal. <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> helps them sign in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send invitation</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.4%;top:49.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:82.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer&#39;s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-mark-a-car-insured-insurer-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: &quot;Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured&quot;. It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the insurer&#39;s email arrives, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark insured</b>. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer&#39;s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One email for several cars? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark several insured</b> on the line &quot; cars wait for the insurer&quot;. Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same button is on the car: Overview (<b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>) and the Listing tab&#39;s checklist, item &quot;Not on the fleet insurance policy yet&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email &quot;Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy&quot;. Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners-who-paid-another-way-and-the-terms-you-agreed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed</h2><p class="gd-p">Two lines on To do keep an owner&#39;s money right without opening their page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Record the first and last month paid by &quot;: their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press <b class="gd-ui">Record what they paid</b>, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car&#39;s invoice is then marked paid, the owner gets the receipt and the two prepaid months count. Never for a shareholder.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Enter the terms agreed with &quot;: their cars still use the standard grid. Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the terms</b>: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to change? Press <b class="gd-ui">Not needed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">These are correct</b>: the line does not come back.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-shareholder-s-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A shareholder&#39;s own car</h2><p class="gd-p">On the owner&#39;s page, each car has <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A shareholder&#39;s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-cancellation-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancellation refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: the refund for each cancellation tier.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When the renter cancels</th><th scope="col">Refund (default)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start</td><td>95%</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before the start</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before the start</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Under 24 hours, or after the start</td><td>0%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> sit under the name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Cars and terms, at the top: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> and History (see An owner&#39;s terms, car by car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car&#39;s terms, for each car whose terms are set.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Owner: address, sign-in, agreements, and what is still missing for the registry forms.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Statements and payouts for this owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Forms C and D, with a link to the review queue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Further down: <b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send a sign-in link to the owner portal</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:410/1030"><img src="/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="410" height="1030"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:24.6%;top:4.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16.1%;top:32.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.5%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.2%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-terms-car-by-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s terms, car by car</h2><p class="gd-p">The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner&#39;s page and its Terms tab: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car&#39;s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not signed yet (or not approved yet): <b class="gd-ui">Save</b> applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings &gt; Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days&#39; written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner&#39;s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car&#39;s History.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Record signed on paper (with the date) and Withdraw it. One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.</p><p class="gd-p">The same editor is on the car&#39;s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner&#39;s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-pay-an-owner-a-flat-monthly-amount" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an owner a flat monthly amount</h2><p class="gd-p">Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Flat monthly payment</b>, type the <b class="gd-ui">Amount a month</b> (for example 900.00), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b> and, if it ends, the <b class="gd-ui">Last day</b>. Write the Reason (kept in the history).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">From that date the owner&#39;s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Back to revenue share: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars&#39; own unless you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge to the owner</b> beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner&#39;s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-change-a-signed-car-s-management-mode" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change a signed car&#39;s Management Mode</h2><p class="gd-p">Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change mode</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">New Management Mode</b> and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b>, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked for this</b> only when it is their own request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars&#39; signature and the owner is emailed the notice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Anything else (CarmaCars&#39; own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. In History, <b class="gd-ui">Record signed on paper</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-paid-and-signed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Paid and signed</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Paid and signed</b> tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checklist and quick actions</b>. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper, Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed on paper? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record paper signature</b>. Choose the Document, check Signed by and Date signed, add the witnesses where the form needs them, and upload the scan of every signed page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same checklist sits at the top of each owner&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with <b class="gd-ui">Record paper signature</b>. Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on &quot; in their portal. A paper signature counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner&#39;s documents.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Forms C and D</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Form C is signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witness on the same screen. Form D (and Form C on paper, if the owner prefers) is printed, signed in front of witnesses, and sent as a photo of each page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/470"><img src="/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="470"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:57.6%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-the-earnings-calculator-on-list-your-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The earnings calculator on List your car</h2><p class="gd-p">People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, &quot;set in your agreement&quot;). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class&#39;s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. &quot;Just cheaper insurance&quot; shows the fleet policy&#39;s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown</b> and <b class="gd-ui">the monthly tracker fee shown</b>, in dollars a month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave either one empty and the page says &quot;Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement&quot; and shows the earnings &quot;before fees&quot;. No amount is ever made up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner&#39;s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owner-money', 'chapter', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner invoices**. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.

1. Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. **Add a line** for more.
2. **Save as draft** to come back to it, or **Save and issue** to send it now. On a draft''s page, **Issue and email** sends it.
3. Paid another way? Press **Record payment** on the invoice. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.
4. **Resend email** sends the invoice again. **PDF** opens it as a PDF.

## Correct an issued invoice

An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.

1. Press **Void**, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press **Void the invoice**. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.
2. The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press **Save and issue**.
3. Already paid? Void the payment first, or press **Credit note** for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.

Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.

## The automatic debit

The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for returned debits and owners without a mandate.

:::flow
Notice day | Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before
Debit day | The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice
Cleared | The invoice is paid
Returned, insufficient funds | The $50.00 Late Fee is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days
Returned for another reason | No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task
:::

1. The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.
2. How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.
3. Scheduled and processing lists each debit. **Pause** holds one (a reason is needed).
4. Owners lists each mandate. Use **Pause**, **Resume** or **Send a notice now**.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 920; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 1 21.8 21.7, 2 21.5 35.5, 3 91.5 75.4, 4 84.7 94.7")

5. Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank''s reason.
6. Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.
7. Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 5 11.0 14.4, 6 10.2 52.3, 7 15.4 89.8")

Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner''s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task.

> Watch out: Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner''s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no mandate gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.

## Owner statements

**Money** > **Owner statements**

1. Press **Build all for a month** (or **Build one**).
2. Open each draft. Check it, **Rebuild** after a correction, **Preview PDF**, then **Approve**.
3. Press **Issue to the owner**. **Reissue** sends a corrected copy; **CSV** exports it.

![](/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 400; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements; pins: 1 79.9 27.3")

![An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.](/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000; pins: 3 86.0 22.7")

## Staff commissions

**Money** > **Staff commissions**. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Not earned yet | The rental is ahead, or not paid in full
Pending approval | Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended
Approved | You approved it; the staff member is told
Paid | You recorded the payment; the staff member is told
Reversed | Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment
:::

1. By person shows each staff member''s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.
2. Press **Approve** on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.
3. Press **Record a payment**: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.
4. **Prices to review** lists prices typed by hand; **Sourcing claims** lists staff who say they sourced a website request; **Payments made** lists each payment.
5. **Owner requests** lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company''s share or of the cars'' rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press **Approve**, **Change and approve** (your terms, with a note) or **Decline**. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner''s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner''s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.
6. Who sourced an owner: the owner''s page, **Sourced by**. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month''s rentals |
| An owner a salesperson brought in | The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars'', a partner''s or a shareholder''s cars |
| Customer service, finance, fleet, field staff | 10% (also the field referral fee) |
| Base | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off |
| On the owner statement | An owner''s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner''s car: from CarmaCars'' commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense |

> Tip: A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month''s Sales tier) goes on the owner''s next statement as an adjustment line.

## Field pay

**Money** > **Field pay**. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Clocked in and out | Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out
Pay run started | Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions
Approved | The figures are frozen, the period''s hours are locked, the statements are numbered
Paid | You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email
:::

1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the pay run**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company statements

CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.
