Clocked in and out | Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out
Pay run started | Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions
Approved | The figures are frozen, the period''s hours are locked, the statements are numbered
Paid | You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email
:::

1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the pay run**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company model

Money > **Company model** is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.

1. **Forecast**: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months'' EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.
2. **Actuals**: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental''s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. **Refresh actuals now** recomputes them at once.
3. **Pro forma 5 years**: each year''s income statement, cash flow and key figures.
4. **Assumptions**: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press **Save the assumptions**; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked "From the actuals" left blank uses the latest complete month.
5. **Download as Excel**: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.

> Tip: Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month''s costs in Money > Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.

## Company statements

**Money** > **Company accounts**, the **Monthly statements** tab: CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-invoices" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner invoices</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Invoices</b> tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner&#39;s and each application&#39;s Invoices tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> makes an invoice of any amount for an owner&#39;s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The monthly run and tracker invoices: <b class="gd-ui">Run the monthly invoices</b> issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); <b class="gd-ui">Issue all tracker invoices</b> bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/invoices</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1060"><img src="/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1060"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:22.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:35.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-make-edit-and-issue-an-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Make, edit and issue an invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. <b class="gd-ui">Add a line</b> for more.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save as draft</b> to come back to it, or <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b> to send it now. On a draft&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Issue and email</b> sends it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid another way? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on the invoice. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend email</b> sends the invoice again. <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b> opens it as a PDF.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-correct-an-issued-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct an issued invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b>, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press <b class="gd-ui">Void the invoice</b>. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already paid? Void the payment first, or press <b class="gd-ui">Credit note</b> for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-the-automatic-debit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The automatic debit</h2><p class="gd-p">The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for returned debits and owners without a mandate.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Notice day</span><em>Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Debit day</span><em>The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Cleared</span><em>The invoice is paid</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Returned, insufficient funds</span><em>The $50.00 Late Fee is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Returned for another reason</span><em>No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Scheduled and processing lists each debit. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b> holds one (a reason is needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners lists each mandate. Use <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Send a notice now</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/920"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="920"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.8%;top:21.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.5%;top:35.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.5%;top:75.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:94.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:14.4%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.4%;top:89.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner&#39;s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner&#39;s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no mandate gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> tab</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Build all for a month</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Build one</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open each draft. Check it, <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> after a correction, <b class="gd-ui">Preview PDF</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Issue to the owner</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Reissue</b> sends a corrected copy; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> exports it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/400"><img src="/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:79.9%;top:27.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg" alt="An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-staff-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff commissions</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff pay</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Commissions</b> tab. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Not earned yet</span><em>The rental is ahead, or not paid in full</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pending approval</span><em>Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>You approved it; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded the payment; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Reversed</span><em>Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">By person shows each staff member&#39;s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Prices to review</b> lists prices typed by hand; <b class="gd-ui">Sourcing claims</b> lists staff who say they sourced a website request; <b class="gd-ui">Payments made</b> lists each payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Owner requests</b> lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company&#39;s share or of the cars&#39; rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change and approve</b> (your terms, with a note) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner&#39;s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner&#39;s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced an owner: the owner&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Sourced by</b>. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month&#39;s rentals</td></tr><tr><td>An owner a salesperson brought in</td><td>The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars&#39;, a partner&#39;s or a shareholder&#39;s cars</td></tr><tr><td>Customer service, finance, fleet, field staff</td><td>10% (also the field referral fee)</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off</td></tr><tr><td>On the owner statement</td><td>An owner&#39;s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner&#39;s car: from CarmaCars&#39; commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month&#39;s Sales tier) goes on the owner&#39;s next statement as an adjustment line.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-field-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff pay</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Field pay</b> tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Clocked in and out</span><em>Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pay run started</span><em>Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>The figures are frozen, the period&#39;s hours are locked, the statements are numbered</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tab <b class="gd-ui">Pay run</b> shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings &gt; Program, Field pay). <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After the period ends, press <b class="gd-ui">Start the pay run</b>: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). <b class="gd-ui">Refresh the figures</b> takes in a change made since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The period&#39;s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (<b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> repeats it). The statement&#39;s number opens its PDF; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> gives the run for your accountant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> lists everyone&#39;s shifts of the period. <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hourly rates</b> shows each person&#39;s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with <b class="gd-ui">Set the rate</b> (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Field pay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overtime</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Vacation pay</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement</td></tr><tr><td>Deductions</td><td>None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer&#39;s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions that net to nothing</td><td>A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-model" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company model</h2><p class="gd-p">Money &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company model</b> is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b>: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months&#39; EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Actuals</b>: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental&#39;s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. <b class="gd-ui">Refresh actuals now</b> recomputes them at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pro forma 5 years</b>: each year&#39;s income statement, cash flow and key figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Assumptions</b>: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the assumptions</b>; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked &quot;From the actuals&quot; left blank uses the latest complete month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download as Excel</b>: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month&#39;s costs in Money &gt; Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company accounts</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Monthly statements</b> tab: CarmaCars&#39; own monthly statement, in twelve sections.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Download <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b>, <b class="gd-ui">PDF by owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">PDF by vehicle</b>, or press <b class="gd-ui">Email me the PDFs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Finalize</b> freezes the month. <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> works until then.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/reports</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:28%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.4%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.1%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.9%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from the revenue statement</h3><p class="gd-p">On an owner&#39;s page, the <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b> button sets <b class="gd-ui">How fees are paid</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Take from revenue statement</b>. Taken from the statement, the owner&#39;s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;. Approved, the invoice reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task <b class="gd-ui">Invoice ... back to the bank debit</b>.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The flat-rate agreements</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b> instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner&#39;s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK</b> is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-how-it-s-paid-bank-debit-or-deducted-from-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How it&#39;s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit on the 15th</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> (taken from the owner&#39;s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On an invoice, <b class="gd-ui">How it&#39;s paid</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For the first and last month, choose <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> on the Terms tab (or at approval).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the Terms tab, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the agreed one-off fees</b> makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner&#39;s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'chapter', 'tolls-and-tickets', 'See who is on the site right now and what they look at, with buying signals, and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers the chat first; you take over whenever you want, and it hands over by itself for complaints, damage, payments and anything it should not answer.

## Live visitors

Visitors who accepted analytics (or got the notice in Canada outside Quebec and the US), known customers on their own booking pages and anyone in a chat.

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**. The map is at the top (see Live map below); under it, **Live now** lists who is on the site now (seen in the last 5 minutes; an open page says it is still there every 45 seconds, so someone reading one page stays on the list), and **History** the visits before (see Past visits below). The line at the top of Live now counts who is live, the visitors today (people, with their visits), hot visitors now, known customers now and chats today. The menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor has an icon for what they are doing (in a chat, a form sent or started, a known customer, on the site); press it, or **Show on the map**, to see them on the map with their card. Filter the list by type, city and source.
2. Visitors who chose necessary cookies only are never recorded: a line under the counts says how many chose that today. Closing the tab takes a visitor off the list at once.
3. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100, with Hot (60 or more), Warm (30 or more) or Cold. The list is sorted by it; choose "Most recent" in Sort, or tick "Hot and warm only".
4. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Reached step 3 of the request form · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals of the visit; the dots say how strong each is.
5. Each visitor also shows their name when known (signed in, or arrived from one of our emails), otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone"; the page and car they are on, and how many others look at that car now; the device, city, the site or campaign that sent them and "from an ad".
6. Suggested: the best next step and the message to send. Press **Invite to chat with this message** to send it at once, **Edit the message** to change it first, **Offer a 10% discount code**, **Assign to Sales** or, when their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car**.
7. Press **Pages** for every page and event of the visit with each signal''s points, or **Start a chat** to write your own message. They see it in a bubble and reply from it.
8. Below: hot visitors today (and whether someone acted), the signals of the last 24 hours, and the most viewed cars of the week with prices shown and the car most compared with each. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), give them a name. Only staff see it.

1. On their line, press **Name**. Type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note. Press **Save the name**.
2. The name shows on Visitors (Live now and History), the visit''s pages and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. The line says who named them, with the phone, email and note.
3. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo, and a call or text from that number shows the name in Texts and calls.
4. Kept consistent: if they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours ("Booked"). A chat from another browser with the same email or phone gets the same name, and a chat''s email or phone fills in the ones you left empty.
5. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Live map

A map of the Greater Toronto Area from Hamilton at the bottom to Barrie at the top, Toronto in the middle, with a dot for every lead, made for a TV or monitor in the office. It reads like a real map: every city and town is outlined (the GTA''s regions, Toronto, Peel, York, Durham, Halton and Hamilton, a little stronger), with the highways and the major roads, the cities'' names, a soft glow where people live and the Niagara Escarpment and the Oak Ridges Moraine as gentle ridges; the lake stays dark and quiet. A lead outside that area widens the map, keeping Toronto in the middle.

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**: the map is at the top. The four numbers: who is on the site now, requests today, cars on rent now and the money collected this month.
2. Each dot is one person, coloured by their stage: green on rent or booked, amber requests and forms (a request, a form sent or a form started), cyan on the site now or a game played, grey past renters. The stages under the map count each one; press one to hide or show it. Renters on rent, bookings and hot leads show as a small card with a photo of their car, framed in their stage colour (the make''s initial when the car has no photo); a hot lead not yet booked has a rose ring. Cards that would cover each other move apart, with a fine line back to their place. Each card and dot carries the person''s first name and last initial ("Visitor in Mississauga" when we do not know who it is). A visitor on the site breathes slowly, a new event sends one ripple, and crowded dots join in a count (press it to zoom in). Busy areas glow softly. The C marker is home base (the delivery origin in **Settings** > **Program**), with a thin line running to each car on rent or booked.
3. Rest the pointer on a lead (a dot or a car card), or move to it with Tab, to preview its card; press it to keep the card open (on a phone or tablet, tap it). The card shows the full name, the stage, the score from 0 to 100 with every signal, the car they looked at last with its photo and daily price, the city, how long they were on the site or when they were last seen, and a link to open the booking, the renter, Live visitors or Renter leads. Press × or Escape to close it. In the list under the map (Live now or History), press a visitor''s icon or **Show on the map** to bring them to the middle of the map with their card.
4. Phones and emails are hidden until you turn on **Show contact** (above the map, and at the top of the side panel in TV mode); the switch works for the map and for the list under it. The choice is remembered on that computer. While it is off, the page never receives them, so a TV left on holds none. Only Admins see them, as on the renter and lead pages.
5. Press **Open TV mode** on the computer connected to the TV and make the browser full screen (F11 on Windows, Control Command F on a Mac). The map fills the screen with the four numbers on top and the stages on On the road''s title line (no pin hides under the numbers or On the road); along the bottom, On the road: the cars on rent and those picked up today, with the renter and when the car is due back (a booking with no car yet shows Car not assigned); on the right, the hottest lead with the car''s photo and the signals that put them there (leads only: never someone on rent or booked; "No hot leads right now" when there is none; changing every 10 seconds) and the live feed, one line per event. Press a lead on the map, in the live feed or in On the road for its card; on the TV the card closes by itself after 20 seconds. It refreshes every 30 seconds and hides the pointer when the mouse is still.

- Where a dot goes: the approximate place of the visitor''s network (about 1 km, from Cloudflare), else the centre of the renter''s home city or of the visit''s city. Nothing is looked up and no address is shown. People with no place are counted under the map.
- The score adds up the points of the signals: what they did (on rent, booking, request, form sent or started), a game played or its prize claimed, past rentals, a returning visit, pages, minutes on the site, cars viewed, on the site now, from an ad, and the strongest Live visitors reasons. 60 or more is hot, 30 or more warm.
- No hardware acceleration: when the browser has WebGL turned off (in Chrome, Settings > System > Use graphics acceleration when available), the same map is drawn another way, a little slower, and a note in the corner says so. Turning hardware acceleration on makes it faster.
- The fleet layer: once CarmaCars'' trackers report, each car shows on the map with its photo, the direction it is going and its status (on rent, available, in service). Tick **Fleet** to show or hide it.

## Past visits (History)

Press **History** under the map for the visits before now: who (a name when we know it), where they came from (the site, the search or the campaign, and "ad"), the first and last page, how many pages and cars, how long, the device and city, and what the visit led to (a request, a booking, an account, contact details). Filter by dates, what it led to, city and source or campaign; **More filters** has the device, the landing page, the country, new or returning, and bots and staff. **Totals and day by day** shows the dates'' visits, conversions, the chart and the top pages and sources. Press a visit''s icon to see it on the map (when it is still there), or **Open the visit** for every page and event. Visitor history and Live visitors are now this one page; their old links open it.

## The signals

Each signal adds points to the booking likelihood. They come from what the visitor does on the site, never from what they type.

- Intent: dates searched again and again, saw the full price, reached the booking form (and which step), came back for the same car on another day, comparing two or three cars, read the cancellation policy, read about the deposit, insurance or requirements, tapped to call, text or WhatsApp us or copied our number, checked delivery, looked through many photos or stayed long on one car.
- Urgency: pickup within 72 hours, weekend or holiday dates, on a phone late at night, came from a city or model page or a "near me" search.
- Value: a weekly or monthly rental, a premium car, SUV or van, adding a driver, asked about young drivers, a business email.
- Hesitation: watching the price (sorted by lowest price, lowered the price limit), left after seeing the price, unsure about the deposit, trouble with a form, the car not free for their dates.
- Context: came from an ad, a past renter, an offer or payment waiting, a game code not used yet, a popular car. The signals of known customers (offer opened, pay page left, change proposal, request stopped, returning visitor, viewing spree) count too.

## Hot visitors and the actions

- When a visitor turns hot, everyone with Live visitors open sees an alert at the top of the page. Turn on desktop alerts in Live chat to get one on your computer too; none come in the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am). No email is sent.
- A discount code is single use, 10% off the rental charge (at most $75), valid 3 days, one per visitor a week and 10 a day per person. Admins and Sales send them; the code goes in the chat with the message.
- Assign to Sales gives the visitor to the Sales person on shift (or to you if you work Sales) and raises a task with the reasons and the contact when we know who they are.
- Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago") so two people do not write to the same visitor.

## Signal settings

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors** and press **Signal settings** (above the Live now list).
2. Score and actions: from how many points a visitor is hot or warm, when a signal is strong or medium, the hot alert, and the discount code (percent, most off a booking, days valid, codes a day per person, whether customer service may send codes, and the message).
3. Each signal: on or off, its points, its thresholds (for example 72 hours for "Pickup soon", 3 searches for "Searching dates again and again"), the suggested action and the message. {car}, {days}, {pickup} and the other words in braces are filled in from the visit.
4. Press **Save the signals**. The next look at each visit uses them.

## Follow-up tasks

Signals of known visitors become tasks with a suggested action, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours".

- An offer opened and not answered: after 6 hours, to Sales when the booking is credited to someone in Sales, otherwise customer service.
- The pay page left without paying: after 30 minutes, customer service. The change proposal opened twice: customer service.
- A booking request started and stopped, or a viewing spree, by a known visitor: Sales.
- A task closes by itself when the renter answers the offer, pays or answers the proposal. Each signal raises one task only.
- The thresholds are in **Settings** > **Program**, group "Live visitors and live chat", with how long "on the site now" lasts (5 minutes) and how often an open page says it is still there (45 seconds). Follow-ups done count in My sales.

## Recovery emails

Known renters who stop before finishing get one polite reminder, and at most one more a day later.

- An offer opened and not answered: after 4 hours. The pay page left without paying: after an hour. A change proposal opened and not answered: after 4 hours.
- A booking request started and not sent: after 2 hours, and only to renters who agreed to hear from us (marketing consent).
- Sent only between 9:00 and 21:00 Toronto time, never to someone who unsubscribed, and never while a staff member is handling the renter (a task they took, a chat with a person, a message from staff).
- They stop as soon as the renter answers, pays or sends the request; a reminder still waiting is not sent. The delays and hours are in Program settings, "Booking recovery emails".

## Interest in a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, a car, Overview: "Interest on the site" shows who is looking now, views today and in 7 days, the people who saw the price for their dates, conversion over 30 days (requests from the people who viewed it), the cars most often compared with it, and the last 14 days. The Vehicles list has "Most viewed cars this week".

## A renter''s visits

On a renter''s page (People > Renters, the name) and on a booking''s History tab, "On the site" lists when they viewed the offer, opened the change proposal, viewed or left the pay page, which cars they looked at, and their chats.

## Live chat

1. A visitor who asks for a person is a line on To do, marked Now: press **Open the chat**. Or open **Bookings** > **Live chat**. The menu counts the chats that need a reply: a chat waiting for a person, or one a person has where the visitor wrote last. Live chat shows the same number. Those chats come first, with their minutes against the first reply target (5 minutes).
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it you see the visitor''s page, pages, signals, and the renter with their bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over**: the assistant stops and the visitor reads that you joined. Writing a reply also takes over. Press **Send** (or Enter).
4. **Hand back to the assistant** lets it answer again. **Close** ends the chat; if the visitor gave an email they get a copy. **Email the transcript** sends it any time.
5. Alerts: each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert to the bell and, with phone alerts on, to your phone (topic Messages), on shift or not. A chat someone has goes to that person only. The alert clears when someone replies or the chat closes. "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" and desktop alerts in this browser are in Notify me.

> Tip: The assistant only repeats prices from our pricing (a quote or the car''s rates), never offers discounts or promises a car, never talks about insurance and never names a provider. Each reply it was not allowed to send says so in the conversation. When nobody is on shift, the chat asks for the visitor''s name, email or phone and raises a task. A booking from a chat you handled is credited only when you choose "I sourced this client" on the quote or offer.

## When the visitor leaves

- A visitor not seen on the site for 10 minutes has left (Settings > Program, "Live chat: a visitor not seen on the site for this many minutes has left").
- No phone or email: the chat closes by itself, marked **Visitor left, no contact**. It leaves the count and its alerts clear.
- A phone or email (typed in the chat, left in the contact box, or on their renter account): the chat stays open as **Follow up by text/email**, out of the count, and customer service gets the task "Follow up by text/email" in their queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done.
- A visitor who comes back to the site opens the chat again where it was.

## When the assistant does not answer

The assistant answers first, within seconds, and asks for a phone number or email early so we can follow up. It hands over when the visitor asks for a person or when it is not sure.

- When it cannot answer, Live chat shows **AI replies paused** with the reason: turned off in Settings, today''s live share of the free AI allowance used, or the last reply failed. The chat goes to a person and the conversation shows a staff note (only staff see it).
- Common questions (the deposit, age and licence, how booking works, cancellation, hours, delivery) are answered from our own facts with no AI use.
- The free AI allowance is shared by tier (open **Settings**, then **Usage**): the staff assistant keeps 30%, live features (visitor chat, the phone line, the readers) have 50%, background writing 10%. Press **Change the shares** to change them.

## The assistant''s settings

In Program settings, "Live visitors and live chat": the chat on or off, the AI first or not (on by default), its model (Llama 3.1 8B), the neurons it may use a day (6,000, a few hundred replies; then chats wait for a person), when a visitor has left (10 minutes), the greeting on car pages after some seconds (off by default), how long chats and visits are kept, as the privacy policy says: chats 12 months, the pages of a visit 90 days, the visit''s summary in History 13 months, and the daily totals, which name no one, 3 years.

## What a visitor typed

A visitor who typed contact details into a form shows them on their line: "Typed into the booking request, not sent: Maya Chen, maya@example.com", with **Email not confirmed** until they open the link we emailed, and **Renter page**.
', 'Live visitors and live chat', 'Who is on the site now and who came before, on the map and in one list (Today > Visitors): how likely each visitor is to book and why, one-click actions, follow-ups, interest per car, the chat inbox, and TV mode for the office.',
  'See who is on the site right now and what they look at, with buying signals, and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers the chat first; you take over whenever you want, and it hands over by itself for complaints, damage, payments and anything it should not answer.

## Live visitors

Visitors who accepted analytics (or got the notice in Canada outside Quebec and the US), known customers on their own booking pages and anyone in a chat.

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**. The map is at the top (see Live map below); under it, **Live now** lists who is on the site now (seen in the last 5 minutes; an open page says it is still there every 45 seconds, so someone reading one page stays on the list), and **History** the visits before (see Past visits below). The line at the top of Live now counts who is live, the visitors today (people, with their visits), hot visitors now, known customers now and chats today. The menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor has an icon for what they are doing (in a chat, a form sent or started, a known customer, on the site); a known person shows what they are to us (Owner, Owner · renter, Investor, Partner, Staff, Renter) from all their records, never just "renter" for an owner; press it, or **Show on the map**, to see them on the map with their card. Filter the list by type, city and source.
2. Visitors who chose necessary cookies only are never recorded: a line under the counts says how many chose that today. Closing the tab takes a visitor off the list at once.
3. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100, with Hot (60 or more), Warm (30 or more) or Cold. The list is sorted by it; choose "Most recent" in Sort, or tick "Hot and warm only".
4. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Reached step 3 of the request form · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals of the visit; the dots say how strong each is.
5. Each visitor also shows their name when known (signed in, or arrived from one of our emails), otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone"; the page and car they are on, and how many others look at that car now; the device, city, the site or campaign that sent them and "from an ad".
6. Suggested: the best next step and the message to send. Press **Invite to chat with this message** to send it at once, **Edit the message** to change it first, **Offer a 10% discount code**, **Assign to Sales** or, when their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car**.
7. Press **Pages** for every page and event of the visit with each signal''s points, or **Start a chat** to write your own message. They see it in a bubble and reply from it.
8. Below: hot visitors today (and whether someone acted), the signals of the last 24 hours, and the most viewed cars of the week with prices shown and the car most compared with each. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), give them a name. Only staff see it.

1. On their line, press **Name**. Type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note. Press **Save the name**.
2. The name shows on Visitors (Live now and History), the visit''s pages and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. The line says who named them, with the phone, email and note.
3. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo, and a call or text from that number shows the name in Texts and calls.
4. Kept consistent: if they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours ("Booked"). A chat from another browser with the same email or phone gets the same name, and a chat''s email or phone fills in the ones you left empty.
5. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Live map

A map of the Greater Toronto Area from Hamilton at the bottom to Barrie at the top, Toronto in the middle, with a dot for every lead, made for a TV or monitor in the office. It reads like a real map: every city and town is outlined (the GTA''s regions, Toronto, Peel, York, Durham, Halton and Hamilton, a little stronger), with the highways and the major roads, the cities'' names, a soft glow where people live and the Niagara Escarpment and the Oak Ridges Moraine as gentle ridges; the lake stays dark and quiet. A lead outside that area widens the map, keeping Toronto in the middle.

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**: the map is at the top. The four numbers: who is on the site now, requests today, cars on rent now and the money collected this month.
2. Each dot is one person, coloured by their stage: green on rent or booked, amber requests and forms (a request, a form sent or a form started), cyan on the site now or a game played, grey past renters. The stages under the map count each one; press one to hide or show it. Renters on rent, bookings and hot leads show as a small card with a photo of their car, framed in their stage colour (the make''s initial when the car has no photo); a hot lead not yet booked has a rose ring. Cards that would cover each other move apart, with a fine line back to their place. Each card and dot carries the person''s first name and last initial ("Visitor in Mississauga" when we do not know who it is). A visitor on the site breathes slowly, a new event sends one ripple, and crowded dots join in a count bubble, coloured by the hottest person in it (press it to zoom in until it splits; people on one spot open as a ring). Names show only for leads and hot visitors, from city zoom up, and pins are a little smaller at city zoom. Busy areas glow softly. The C marker is home base (the delivery origin in **Settings** > **Program**), with a thin line running to each car on rent or booked.
3. Rest the pointer on a lead (a dot or a car card), or move to it with Tab, to preview its card; press it to keep the card open (on a phone or tablet, tap it). The card shows the full name, the stage, the score from 0 to 100 with every signal, the car they looked at last with its photo and daily price, the city, how long they were on the site or when they were last seen, and a link to open the booking, the renter, Live visitors or Renter leads. Press × or Escape to close it. In the list under the map (Live now or History), press a visitor''s icon or **Show on the map** to bring them to the middle of the map with their card.
4. Phones and emails are hidden until you turn on **Show contact** (above the map, and at the top of the side panel in TV mode); the switch works for the map and for the list under it. The choice is remembered on that computer. While it is off, the page never receives them, so a TV left on holds none. Only Admins see them, as on the renter and lead pages.
5. Press **Open TV mode** on the computer connected to the TV and make the browser full screen (F11 on Windows, Control Command F on a Mac). The map fills the screen with the four numbers on top and the stages on On the road''s title line (no pin hides under the numbers or On the road); along the bottom, On the road: the cars on rent and those picked up today, with the renter and when the car is due back (a booking with no car yet shows Car not assigned); on the right, the hottest lead with the car''s photo and the signals that put them there (leads only: never someone on rent or booked; "No hot leads right now" when there is none; changing every 10 seconds) and the live feed, one line per event. Press a lead on the map, in the live feed or in On the road for its card; on the TV the card closes by itself after 20 seconds. It refreshes every 30 seconds and hides the pointer when the mouse is still.

- Where a dot goes: the approximate place of the visitor''s network (about 1 km, from Cloudflare), else the centre of the renter''s home city or of the visit''s city. Nothing is looked up and no address is shown. People with no place are counted under the map.
- The score adds up the points of the signals: what they did (on rent, booking, request, form sent or started), a game played or its prize claimed, past rentals, a returning visit, pages, minutes on the site, cars viewed, on the site now, from an ad, and the strongest Live visitors reasons. 60 or more is hot, 30 or more warm.
- No hardware acceleration: when the browser has WebGL turned off (in Chrome, Settings > System > Use graphics acceleration when available), the same map is drawn another way, a little slower, and a note in the corner says so. Turning hardware acceleration on makes it faster.
- The fleet layer: once CarmaCars'' trackers report, each car shows on the map with its photo, the direction it is going and its status (on rent, available, in service). Tick **Fleet** to show or hide it.

## Past visits (History)

Press **History** under the map for the visits before now, in one list grouped by day (Today, Yesterday, then the date). Each visit is one row: the time, who (a name when we know it, with what they are to us: Owner, Owner · renter, Investor, Partner, Staff or Renter), the city, where they came from (ad, search, direct), the pages and small photos of the cars they looked at (up to 3 and "+n"), a dot for the score and what it led to (Request sent, Booked, Account, Lead, Chat or Left). Press a row for the pages in order, how long and where; **Open the visit** has every page and event, and **Show on the map** finds them there when they are still on it. Pick **Today**, **7 days**, **30 days** or **90 days** to set the dates in one press, or **Custom** to type them; the Source and Led to filters are next to the dates and **More filters** has the city, the device, the landing page, the country, new or returning, and bots and staff. The search box above the list narrows the rows on the page. One line shows the totals; **Day by day and top pages** opens the chart and the top lists. Visitor history and Live visitors are now this one page; their old links open it.

## The signals

Each signal adds points to the booking likelihood. They come from what the visitor does on the site, never from what they type.

- Intent: dates searched again and again, saw the full price, reached the booking form (and which step), came back for the same car on another day, comparing two or three cars, read the cancellation policy, read about the deposit, insurance or requirements, tapped to call, text or WhatsApp us or copied our number, checked delivery, looked through many photos or stayed long on one car.
- Urgency: pickup within 72 hours, weekend or holiday dates, on a phone late at night, came from a city or model page or a "near me" search.
- Value: a weekly or monthly rental, a premium car, SUV or van, adding a driver, asked about young drivers, a business email.
- Hesitation: watching the price (sorted by lowest price, lowered the price limit), left after seeing the price, unsure about the deposit, trouble with a form, the car not free for their dates.
- Context: came from an ad, a past renter, an offer or payment waiting, a game code not used yet, a popular car. The signals of known customers (offer opened, pay page left, change proposal, request stopped, returning visitor, viewing spree) count too.

## Hot visitors and the actions

- When a visitor turns hot, everyone with Live visitors open sees an alert at the top of the page. Turn on desktop alerts in Live chat to get one on your computer too; none come in the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am). No email is sent.
- A discount code is single use, 10% off the rental charge (at most $75), valid 3 days, one per visitor a week and 10 a day per person. Admins and Sales send them; the code goes in the chat with the message.
- Assign to Sales gives the visitor to the Sales person on shift (or to you if you work Sales) and raises a task with the reasons and the contact when we know who they are.
- Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago") so two people do not write to the same visitor.

## Signal settings

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors** and press **Signal settings** (above the Live now list).
2. Score and actions: from how many points a visitor is hot or warm, when a signal is strong or medium, the hot alert, and the discount code (percent, most off a booking, days valid, codes a day per person, whether customer service may send codes, and the message).
3. Each signal: on or off, its points, its thresholds (for example 72 hours for "Pickup soon", 3 searches for "Searching dates again and again"), the suggested action and the message. {car}, {days}, {pickup} and the other words in braces are filled in from the visit.
4. Press **Save the signals**. The next look at each visit uses them.

## Follow-up tasks

Signals of known visitors become tasks with a suggested action, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours".

- An offer opened and not answered: after 6 hours, to Sales when the booking is credited to someone in Sales, otherwise customer service.
- The pay page left without paying: after 30 minutes, customer service. The change proposal opened twice: customer service.
- A booking request started and stopped, or a viewing spree, by a known visitor: Sales.
- A task closes by itself when the renter answers the offer, pays or answers the proposal. Each signal raises one task only.
- The thresholds are in **Settings** > **Program**, group "Live visitors and live chat", with how long "on the site now" lasts (5 minutes) and how often an open page says it is still there (45 seconds). Follow-ups done count in My sales.

## Recovery emails

Known renters who stop before finishing get one polite reminder, and at most one more a day later.

- An offer opened and not answered: after 4 hours. The pay page left without paying: after an hour. A change proposal opened and not answered: after 4 hours.
- A booking request started and not sent: after 2 hours, and only to renters who agreed to hear from us (marketing consent).
- Sent only between 9:00 and 21:00 Toronto time, never to someone who unsubscribed, and never while a staff member is handling the renter (a task they took, a chat with a person, a message from staff).
- They stop as soon as the renter answers, pays or sends the request; a reminder still waiting is not sent. The delays and hours are in Program settings, "Booking recovery emails".

## Interest in a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, a car, Overview: "Interest on the site" shows who is looking now, views today and in 7 days, the people who saw the price for their dates, conversion over 30 days (requests from the people who viewed it), the cars most often compared with it, and the last 14 days. The Vehicles list has "Most viewed cars this week".

## A renter''s visits

On a renter''s page (People > Renters, the name) and on a booking''s History tab, "On the site" lists when they viewed the offer, opened the change proposal, viewed or left the pay page, which cars they looked at, and their chats.

## Live chat

1. A visitor who asks for a person is a line on To do, marked Now: press **Open the chat**. Or open **Bookings** > **Live chat**. The menu counts the chats that need a reply: a chat waiting for a person, or one a person has where the visitor wrote last. Live chat shows the same number. Those chats come first, with their minutes against the first reply target (5 minutes).
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it you see the visitor''s page, pages, signals, and the renter with their bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over**: the assistant stops and the visitor reads that you joined. Writing a reply also takes over. Press **Send** (or Enter).
4. **Hand back to the assistant** lets it answer again. **Close** ends the chat; if the visitor gave an email they get a copy. **Email the transcript** sends it any time.
5. Alerts: each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert to the bell and, with phone alerts on, to your phone (topic Messages), on shift or not. A chat someone has goes to that person only. The alert clears when someone replies or the chat closes. "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" and desktop alerts in this browser are in Notify me.

> Tip: The assistant only repeats prices from our pricing (a quote or the car''s rates), never offers discounts or promises a car, never talks about insurance and never names a provider. Each reply it was not allowed to send says so in the conversation. When nobody is on shift, the chat asks for the visitor''s name, email or phone and raises a task. A booking from a chat you handled is credited only when you choose "I sourced this client" on the quote or offer.

## When the visitor leaves

- A visitor not seen on the site for 10 minutes has left (Settings > Program, "Live chat: a visitor not seen on the site for this many minutes has left").
- No phone or email: the chat closes by itself, marked **Visitor left, no contact**. It leaves the count and its alerts clear.
- A phone or email (typed in the chat, left in the contact box, or on their renter account): the chat stays open as **Follow up by text/email**, out of the count, and customer service gets the task "Follow up by text/email" in their queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done.
- A visitor who comes back to the site opens the chat again where it was.

