  '<p class="gd-p">You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.</p><p class="gd-p">Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.</p><section class="gd-task" id="sales-requests-offers-and-new-quotes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests, offers and new quotes</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Requests and offers</b>: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under &quot;more not open to you yet&quot;, with the time it opens to you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>: <b class="gd-ui">My bookings</b>, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b>: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> still makes a request to offer later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An offer that is out: <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/580"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="580"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:39.8%;top:59.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the &quot;Quote sent&quot; measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-check-the-renter-s-licence" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check the renter&#39;s licence</h2><p class="gd-p">Sales approve the renter&#39;s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Licences to check</b> lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review the licence</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking, the card <b class="gd-ui">Renter licence</b> has the same: press <b class="gd-ui">Review the licence</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Look at each image: the name and date of birth match the booking, class G2 or G, valid past the return, no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>. The renter is told and asked for a new image.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">In person (Toronto)</th><th scope="col">Remote (anywhere)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Commission</td><td>Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%</td><td>Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source</td><td>Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>You choose</td><td>At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you</td></tr><tr><td>Every day</td><td>Nothing set</td><td>Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach</td></tr><tr><td>Every month</td><td>Nothing set</td><td>400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-remote-your-duties" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Remote: your duties</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remote duties</b> shows this month&#39;s touches against 400, today&#39;s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">For anything else press <b class="gd-ui">Log a touch</b>: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist ticks itself as the day&#39;s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under My availability choose this week or next, press <b class="gd-ui">Add a block</b> for each time you will be on, then <b class="gd-ui">Save the week</b>. Days already past stay as they were.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-my-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My sales</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Me</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b> tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press <b class="gd-ui">By month</b> for months, <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> for weeks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to you</td><td>A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else.</td></tr><tr><td>Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added</td><td>Counted on the day they happened.</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings confirmed, booked revenue</td><td>Counted on the day the booking was confirmed.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr><tr><td>Rental days (Sales)</td><td>The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month&#39;s tier applies to all of that month&#39;s rentals.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month&#39;s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-owners-you-bring-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners you bring in</h2><p class="gd-p">Bring in car owners on <b class="gd-ui">My work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b>, card <b class="gd-ui">Owners you bring in</b>. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as &quot;sourced by&quot;, with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite an owner</b>: enter their name, email and phone, tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked me to send it</b>, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the invitation</b>. They get an email with your link to apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Copy my owner link</b>: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Start an application</b>: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin&#39;s.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The row of five figures follows your owners: <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Applied</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approved</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Car live</b> and <b class="gd-ui">First paid rental</b>. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task &quot;Unfinished owner application&quot; and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-ask-for-your-commission-on-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ask for your commission on an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the owner&#39;s row press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a commission</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">A flat amount</b> and type it, or <b class="gd-ui">A percent</b>: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company&#39;s share of their cars&#39; rentals, or their cars&#39; rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send to an Admin</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">While it waits you can press <b class="gd-ui">Change my request</b>. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Approved as</th><th scope="col">When it is earned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A flat amount</td><td>Once, at the owner&#39;s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full</td></tr><tr><td>A percent</td><td>On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars&#39; own cars, a partner&#39;s, a shareholder&#39;s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-buyer-leads" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Buyer leads</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Buyer leads</b>: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours, then call them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owners you bring in</b>, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'academy', 'chapter', 'commissions', 'Your training path is under **My work** > **Academy** (field work: **Field work** > **Academy**). There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. If the academy gate is on, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths; the guide and your profile stay open.', 'Academy', 'Your training path: lessons narrated by your browser, a quiz per section, 80% to pass.',
