3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. If the academy gate is on, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths; the guide and your profile stay open.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your training path is under <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-watch-the-lessons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Watch the lessons</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser&#39;s own voice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> move through the scenes; <b class="gd-ui">Replay</b> starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. <b class="gd-ui">Voice on</b> turns the voice off and on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser&#39;s, so it can sound different on another device.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-pass-the-quiz" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pass the quiz</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under the lessons, answer every question and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my answers</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b> as often as you need.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. If the academy gate is on, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths; the guide and your profile stay open.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Customer service and Sales see who is on the site now and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers first; you take over whenever you want.

## Live visitors

1. Open **Live** > **Live visitors**. "Live now" counts who is on the site now, "Visitors today" the people seen today. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds; the menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100 (Hot, Warm or Cold); the most likely to book come first.
2. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Saw $320 for 3 days · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals; the dots say how strong each is.
3. Each visitor shows a name when known, otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone", the page and car they are on, how many others look at that car now, and this visit''s pages.
4. Suggested: the next step and a message. Press **Invite to chat with this message**, or **Edit the message** first. Sales can **Offer a 10% discount code** (one per visitor a week). **Assign to Sales** hands the visitor to Sales with a task. When their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car** writes the message for you.
5. Press **Pages** for the whole visit. Press **Start a chat** to write your own short friendly message and press **Send**: the visitor sees it in a bubble.
6. A hot visitor raises an alert at the top of the page. Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago"), so check it before writing.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), press **Name** on their line, type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note, then press **Save the name**. The name shows on Live visitors, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. Only staff see it. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo. If they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Follow-ups

Signals of known visitors raise tasks on To do with what to do, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours". Call or message, then mark the task done. A task closes by itself when the renter answers or pays. Follow-ups done count in My sales.

Renters also get one polite reminder email (and at most one more) when they leave an offer, the pay page or a change unanswered. Taking the follow-up task, a chat with you or a message from you stops these reminders: you are handling it.

## Live chat

1. Open **Live** > **Live chat**. The menu counts the chats that need a reply (waiting for a person, or the visitor wrote last). Reply within 5 minutes.
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it: the visitor''s page, pages and signals, and the renter''s bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over** (or just write a reply): the assistant stops. Write and press **Send** or Enter. The visitor sees when you type.
4. **Hand back to the assistant** when you are done, or **Close**. A visitor who gave an email gets a copy of the chat.
5. Each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert (the bell, and your phone with phone alerts on). Tick "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" or desktop alerts if you want them too.
6. A visitor who left the site for 10 minutes: with no phone or email the chat closes (**Visitor left, no contact**); with one it shows **Follow up by text/email** and the task is in your queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done. If they come back, the chat opens again.
7. **AI replies paused** at the top says why the assistant is not answering; a staff note in the chat says the same. Answer the visitor yourself.

> Tip: Prices: send a quote from New quote, never a price from memory. If you handled the chat, choose "I sourced this client" on the quote; nothing is credited by itself.', 'Live visitors and live chat', 'Who is on the site, how likely each visitor is to book, one-click actions, follow-ups, the chat inbox.',
  'Customer service and Sales see who is on the site now and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers first; you take over whenever you want.

## Live visitors

1. Open **Live visitors** (customer service; Sales: **More sales**). "Live now" counts who is on the site now, "Visitors today" the people seen today. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds; the menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100 (Hot, Warm or Cold); the most likely to book come first.
2. "Why" gives the three strongest reasons, for example "Pickup tomorrow · Saw $320 for 3 days · Tapped to call". The badges are all the signals; the dots say how strong each is.
3. Each visitor shows a name when known, otherwise "Visitor from Toronto, phone", the page and car they are on, how many others look at that car now, and this visit''s pages.
4. Suggested: the next step and a message. Press **Invite to chat with this message**, or **Edit the message** first. Sales can **Offer a 10% discount code** (one per visitor a week). **Assign to Sales** hands the visitor to Sales with a task. When their dates are taken, **Suggest a similar free car** writes the message for you.
5. Press **Pages** for the whole visit. Press **Start a chat** to write your own short friendly message and press **Send**: the visitor sees it in a bubble.
6. A hot visitor raises an alert at the top of the page. Each action shows on the visitor ("Invited by Lena, 2 min ago"), so check it before writing.

## Name a visitor

When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), press **Name** on their line, type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note, then press **Save the name**. The name shows on Live visitors, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. Only staff see it. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo. If they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours. **Edit name** changes it; **Remove the name** takes it off.

## Follow-ups

Signals of known visitors raise tasks on To do with what to do, for example "Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours". Call or message, then mark the task done. A task closes by itself when the renter answers or pays. Follow-ups done count in My sales.

Renters also get one polite reminder email (and at most one more) when they leave an offer, the pay page or a change unanswered. Taking the follow-up task, a chat with you or a message from you stops these reminders: you are handling it.

## Live chat

1. Open **Live chat**. The menu counts the chats that need a reply (waiting for a person, or the visitor wrote last). Reply within 5 minutes.
2. Choose a conversation. Beside it: the visitor''s page, pages and signals, and the renter''s bookings when known.
3. Press **Take over** (or just write a reply): the assistant stops. Write and press **Send** or Enter. The visitor sees when you type.
4. **Hand back to the assistant** when you are done, or **Close**. A visitor who gave an email gets a copy of the chat.
5. Each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert (the bell, and your phone with phone alerts on). Tick "Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)" or desktop alerts if you want them too.
6. A visitor who left the site for 10 minutes: with no phone or email the chat closes (**Visitor left, no contact**); with one it shows **Follow up by text/email** and the task is in your queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done. If they come back, the chat opens again.
7. **AI replies paused** at the top says why the assistant is not answering; a staff note in the chat says the same. Answer the visitor yourself.

> Tip: Prices: send a quote from New quote, never a price from memory. If you handled the chat, choose "I sourced this client" on the quote; nothing is credited by itself.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Customer service and Sales see who is on the site now and answer the live chat. The CarmaCars assistant answers first; you take over whenever you want.</p><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-visitors" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live visitors</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Live visitors</b> (customer service; Sales: <b class="gd-ui">More sales</b>). &quot;Live now&quot; counts who is on the site now, &quot;Visitors today&quot; the people seen today. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds; the menu shows how many hot visitors are on the site. Each visitor shows a booking likelihood from 0 to 100 (Hot, Warm or Cold); the most likely to book come first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Why&quot; gives the three strongest reasons, for example &quot;Pickup tomorrow · Saw $320 for 3 days · Tapped to call&quot;. The badges are all the signals; the dots say how strong each is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each visitor shows a name when known, otherwise &quot;Visitor from Toronto, phone&quot;, the page and car they are on, how many others look at that car now, and this visit&#39;s pages.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Suggested: the next step and a message. Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to chat with this message</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Edit the message</b> first. Sales can <b class="gd-ui">Offer a 10% discount code</b> (one per visitor a week). <b class="gd-ui">Assign to Sales</b> hands the visitor to Sales with a task. When their dates are taken, <b class="gd-ui">Suggest a similar free car</b> writes the message for you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Pages</b> for the whole visit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a chat</b> to write your own short friendly message and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>: the visitor sees it in a bubble.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A hot visitor raises an alert at the top of the page. Each action shows on the visitor (&quot;Invited by Lena, 2 min ago&quot;), so check it before writing.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-name-a-visitor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Name a visitor</h2><p class="gd-p">When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), press <b class="gd-ui">Name</b> on their line, type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the name</b>. The name shows on Live visitors, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. Only staff see it. A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo. If they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours. <b class="gd-ui">Edit name</b> changes it; <b class="gd-ui">Remove the name</b> takes it off.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-follow-ups" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Follow-ups</h2><p class="gd-p">Signals of known visitors raise tasks on To do with what to do, for example &quot;Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours&quot;. Call or message, then mark the task done. A task closes by itself when the renter answers or pays. Follow-ups done count in My sales.</p><p class="gd-p">Renters also get one polite reminder email (and at most one more) when they leave an offer, the pay page or a change unanswered. Taking the follow-up task, a chat with you or a message from you stops these reminders: you are handling it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-chat" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live chat</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Live chat</b>. The menu counts the chats that need a reply (waiting for a person, or the visitor wrote last). Reply within 5 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a conversation. Beside it: the visitor&#39;s page, pages and signals, and the renter&#39;s bookings when known.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b> (or just write a reply): the assistant stops. Write and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> or Enter. The visitor sees when you type.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hand back to the assistant</b> when you are done, or <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>. A visitor who gave an email gets a copy of the chat.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert (the bell, and your phone with phone alerts on). Tick &quot;Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)&quot; or desktop alerts if you want them too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A visitor who left the site for 10 minutes: with no phone or email the chat closes (<b class="gd-ui">Visitor left, no contact</b>); with one it shows <b class="gd-ui">Follow up by text/email</b> and the task is in your queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done. If they come back, the chat opens again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">AI replies paused</b> at the top says why the assistant is not answering; a staff note in the chat says the same. Answer the visitor yourself.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Prices: send a quote from New quote, never a price from memory. If you handled the chat, choose &quot;I sourced this client&quot; on the quote; nothing is credited by itself.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'texts-and-calls', 'chapter', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'Customer service and Sales answer texts to the CarmaCars number in the same place as live chat. Every call and text is kept with the renter, owner or lead it belongs to.

## Answer a text

1. Open **Live** > **Live chat** and press **Texts and calls**. Unread texts and missed calls are counted on each number.
2. Choose a number: calls and texts in order, and beside them who it is, with their bookings.
3. Write the text and press **Send text**. It goes from the CarmaCars number.
4. **Suggest a reply** writes a draft into the box. Read it and change it: it is never sent until you press Send text.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. Type the name if they told you and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** their name.

Quo''s contacts follow the site: everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, added or updated within about five minutes. Change a name or number on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.

## Missed calls

A missed call gives you the task "Missed call from ..." when you have Live chat or Texts and calls open; otherwise it waits in the customer service queue. Call back with the Call button, or text, then mark the task done. Quo itself texts the caller back, so do not send the same message again.

> Tip: A number that texted STOP gets no texts from us, booking texts included, until they text START. Prices go in a quote, never in a text from memory.

## Email, text or both

Each renter and owner chooses how we reach them. Their page in Admin shows it under How we reach them; ask an Admin, or change it there if you can open the page. Texts need a phone they verified with a code. Your own choice is on your Profile, under Messages.
', 'Texts and calls', 'Reading and answering texts, suggestions, unknown callers and missed calls.',
