rning</td><td>How many days of the month the amount earned, for example 31 of 31.</td></tr><tr><td>Next Payment Date</td><td>When the next return is paid: the 15th of the month after the Return Month.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="how-your-returns-work-notices-from-carmacars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Notices from CarmaCars</h2><p class="gd-p">Two notices can appear on Home, under Needs you now, at the top:</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Notice</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Return on hold:</td><td>A return is held, with the reason, for example tax information we still need. Send what it asks for and we release it.</td></tr><tr><td>Redemption notice:</td><td>CarmaCars will repay an amount, with the Redemption Date.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="how-your-returns-work-emails-you-get-from-us" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Emails you get from us</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your statement is ready, with the PDF attached, each month.</li><li>Your return was paid, with the amount and date (not sent when it is reinvested).</li><li>We received your notice: an election change, a bank account change or a contact change.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Our investor emails are servicing notices about your existing investment. They are not an offer or a solicitation. CarmaCars gives no tax advice.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="how-your-returns-work-texts-or-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts or email</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>, under <b class="gd-ui">Messages</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Both</b>. Texts need a phone you verified with a code and link to the page. Statements are always emailed. Reply STOP to any text to stop them.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'the-investor-deck', 'chapter', 'how-your-returns-work', 'The investor deck tells the CarmaCars story in slides: the problem we solve, how the business makes money, every feature of the platform with its real screen, the investment offer, its risks, and how your Return builds.

## Open the deck

1. On **Investments**, press **Open the deck**, or press **Investor deck** in the menu.
2. Above the slides, **Watch the deck** plays the whole deck, narrated, in a few minutes, with captions in the player (it is there once CarmaCars has published the video).
3. Move with **Previous** and **Next**, the arrow keys, or a swipe left or right on a phone. The list at the top jumps to any slide.
4. Press **Download PDF** to save or print it: each slide prints on its own landscape page.

## The calculator

1. Enter an amount (at least the minimum investment) and choose **Paid monthly**, **Reinvested** or **Reinvest, then paid**.
2. Choose how many years to show and the Investment Date.
3. You see when the lockup ends, your first payment date, what a full month pays, what is paid to you for the period, and your Invested Amount at the end, with a chart and a month-by-month table.

The calculator follows your agreement exactly: no Return for the lockup, then one twelfth of the Yearly Percentage on the Invested Amount each month, by days for a part month, paid on the 15th of the next month or added to the Invested Amount at month end.

> Good to know: The examples use the yearly percentage of our current offer. Your own percentage is the one in your agreement. Every example and figure in the deck is an illustration, not a forecast or a promise, and is not part of any offering memorandum.
', 'The investor deck', 'What CarmaCars built, how it makes money, and a calculator for your Return.',
